    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193025": {
      "title": "Surgery, Plastic Surgery, Breast Reconstruction, Microsurgery, Associate Professor/ Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Apply - Interfolio undefined page loaded Skip to Main Content Already have an account? Sign In Surgery, Plastic Surgery, Breast Reconstruction, Microsurgery, Associate Professor/ Assistant Professor Yale University: School of Medicine: Surgery: Plastic Surgery Location New Haven, CT Open Date Sep 04, 2026 Deadline Sep 03, 2028 at 11:59 PM Eastern Time Description Department of Surgery, Division of Surgical Oncology Yale University, School of Medicine The Department of Surgery, Division of Plastic and Reconstructive Surgery at the Yale School of Medicine, is currently seeking a board eligible/board-certified plastic surgeon with expertise in breast reconstruction and microsurgery to join our growing team and serve as Section Chief, Breast Reconstruction . We are seeking an Associate Professor/ Assistant Professor level candidate; rank will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. In addition to clinical duties, our faculty members provide educational training to medical students, residents, and fellows and actively contribute to the academic and research missions of the Department. Applicants should expect to work in a collegial and collaborative environment providing patient-centered care in a multidisciplinary fashion. The successful candidate will provide leadership for the breast reconstruction program and work closely with Breast Surgical Oncology and colleagues across Smilow Cancer Hospital and Yale Cancer Center to further strengthen and grow Yale’s comprehensive breast reconstruction program. Qualifications Yale Medicine has a wide referral network of primary and specialty care physicians throughout Connecticut and the region. We are seeking candidates with an academic orientation in clinical care, research, and education and demonstrated expertise in reconstructive breast surgery, including microsurgical and implant-based reconstruction. Candidates will join a world-class multidisciplinary breast team at the NCI-Designated Comprehensive Cancer Center at Smilow Cancer Hospital at Yale New Haven and Yale Cancer Center. Candidates should have exceptional interpersonal and leadership skills and a commitment to advancing the field of breast reconstruction. In addition to program planning and development, candidates should have experience in quality improvement, education, multidisciplinary collaboration, and operational development. Application Instructions All application materials should be submitted electronically to: http://apply.interfolio.com/ 193025 Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Should you have any questions, please reach out to: Name: Maren Crawford Title: Senior Physician Recruiter, Department of Surgery Email: maren.crawford@yale.edu Phone/Text: 475-339-6083 Application Process This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct\n            this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier\n            account and can send all application materials, including\n            confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. Apply Now Equal Employment Opportunity Statement The University is committed to basing judgments concerning the admission, education, and employment of individuals upon their qualifications and abilities and seeks to attract to its faculty, staff, and student body qualified persons from a broad range of backgrounds and perspectives. Additionally, in accordance with this Policy and as delineated by federal and Connecticut law, Yale does not discriminate in admissions, educational programs, or employment against any individual on account of that individual’s sex; sexual orientation; gender identity or expression; pregnancy, childbirth or related conditions; race; color; national or ethnic origin; religion; age; disability; protected veteran status, or other protected classes as set forth in federal and Connecticut law. Professional Conduct Review for New Faculty Hires The final candidate, upon acceptance of a contingent offer of employment/faculty appointment, may be required to disclose whether they are, or have been, the subject of any disciplinary proceeding (investigation, hearing, etc.) at previous institutions or employers, and may also be subject to a background screening. Candidates who materially misrepresent information on their resume or other application materials are ineligible for hire/appointment. Final candidates may also be required to sign a release to allow Yale to solicit information regarding any substantiated conduct violations from current and/or past employers. © 2026 Elsevier Inc. or its licensors and contributors. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies. Support | Careers | Accessibility Policy | Cookies Settings | Privacy Policy | Terms of Service We use cookies that are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyze, improve, and personalize our content and your digital experience. You can manage your cookie preferences using the Cookie settings link. For more information, see our Cookie Policy Cookie settings Accept all cookies Opt-Out Request Honored Cookie Preference Center We use cookies which are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyse, improve and personalise our content and your digital experience. For more information, see our Cookie Policy and the list of Google Ad-Tech Vendors . You may choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types may impact your experience of our site and the services we are able to offer. See the different category headings below to find out more or change your settings. You may also be able to exercise your privacy choices as described in our Privacy Policy Allow all Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Always active These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off